  "id": "COMPOUND:757 - PROTEIN:5275",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that etoposide may interact with LB831-BLC through multiple indirect pathways, all involving different molecular targets. The first pathway links etoposide to Leukocyte common antigen, which is targeted by Mollicellin N, and ultimately to LB831-BLC. The second pathway connects etoposide to a different compound, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets LB831-BLC. The third pathway involves etoposide interacting with P2X purinoceptor 7, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to LB831-BLC. These pathways collectively indicate that etoposide may exert its effects on LB831-BLC through diverse molecular mechanisms, possibly involving different receptor or enzyme targets. The integration of these pathways suggests that etoposide could act as a broad-acting compound, influencing LB831-BLC through multiple distinct molecular interactions.",
